---
import { assets, originalInsights } from '../product-assets';
interface Props { landing?: boolean }
const { landing=false }=Astro.props;
---
<section class="insights-section" id="insights">
<div class="wrap insights-layout">
<div class="section-copy">
<p class="eyebrow">DISCOVER CATCH INSIGHTS</p>
<h2>{landing ? <>The more you record,<br />
<em>the more you can see.</em>
</> : <>Your journal becomes<br />
<em>your insights.</em>
</>}</h2>
<p>Look back at personal records, your most recorded species and the places in your fishing history.</p>
<p class="quiet">Based on your recorded catches. Views develop as your journal grows; some need enough data.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="#questions">What can Insights tell me? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a>
</div>
<div class="insights-proof">
<figure>
<div class="screen">
<img src={assets["personal-records.jpg"].src} alt="Existing published Personal Records screenshot, showing a Brown Trout personal record and a Common Bream entry." width="709" height="1536" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
</div>
<figcaption>Personal Records · published example</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure>
<div class="screen">
<img src={assets["insights-overview.jpg"].src} alt="Existing published Catch Insights overview with recorded species, locations and recent activity." width="709" height="1536" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
</div>
<figcaption>Catch Insights · published example</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<a class="mobile-insights-link" href={originalInsights.src}>View the Catch Insights example ↗</a>
</div>
<div class="insights-foot wrap">
<span>Personal records</span>
<span>Recorded species</span>
<span>Fishing history</span>
<p>Your catches tell a story. They don’t measure catch rates or fishing effort.</p>
</div>
</section>
